\section{What is reconstructed, and what is refused}{


A phase is in the model when its intercept row (\code{E0}, \code{C0}, \code{L0}) carries
\verb{_STATUS_ = 1}, which is the test \verb{PROC HAZPRED} itself applies. The early
phase becomes \code{hzr_phase("cdf")} and the late phase \code{hzr_phase("g3")}, with
the shape estimates read off the \code{DELTA}/\code{THALF}/\code{NU}/\code{M} and
\code{TAU}/\code{GAMMA}/\code{ALPHA}/\code{ETA} rows.

